[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:53. Hot Snake]
[00:00.320]Passage 53 | 文章五十三
[00:02.055]Hot Snake | 炽热的蛇
[00:04.655]At last firemen have put out a big forest fire in California. | 消防员终于扑灭了加利福尼亚州的一场大森林火灾。
[00:10.660]Since then, they have been trying to find out how the fire began. | 从那时起，他们一直在试图找出火灾是如何开始的。
[00:16.205]Forest fires are often caused by broken glass or by cigarette ends which people carelessly throw away. | 森林火灾通常是由碎玻璃或人们随意丢弃的烟头引起的。
[00:24.920]Yesterday, the firemen examined the ground carefully, but were not able to find any broken glass. | 昨天，消防员仔细检查了地面，但没有发现任何碎玻璃。
[00:32.810]They were also quite sure that a cigarette end did not start the fire. | 他们也相当确定火灾不是由烟头引起的。
[00:39.205]This morning, however, a fireman accidentally discovered the cause. | 然而，今天早上，一名消防员偶然发现了原因。
[00:45.440]He noticed the remains of a snake which was wound around the electric wires of a 16,000 volt power line. | 他注意到了一条蛇的尸体，它缠绕在一条16000伏特电力线的电线上。
[00:55.450]In this way, he was able to solve the mystery. | 通过这种方式，他解开了这个谜团。
[00:59.695]The explanation was simple, but very unusual. | 解释很简单，但非常不寻常。
[01:04.315]A bird had snatched up the snake from the ground and then dropped it onto the wires. | 一只鸟从地上抓起了蛇，然后把它扔到了电线上。
[01:11.765]The snake then wound itself round the wires. | 然后这条蛇把自己缠绕在电线上。
[01:15.780]When it did so, it sent sparks down to the ground and these immediately started a fire. | 当它这样做时，它向地面发出了火花，这些火花立即引起了火灾。